From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 13:23:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: create a dynamic IFC session for a receiving application

The dynamic IFC code creates a session in its tcp_sendmsg probe, when
a listed application sends on an established socket. An iperf3 server
on the device never sends on its data socket, so an upload from a LAN
host to it got no session, no IFC rule and no LRO ring; the flow
stayed on the metered default ring at about 100 Mbit/s. A download to
a local iperf3 client got a session, because the client sends on its
data socket when the stream starts.

The tcp_recvmsg probe now creates the session too, when a listed
application reads from an established socket. That probe already
exists for the copy skip and is shared with the wifi local-in code,
so a flag limits the new work to the time the dynamic IFC probes are
registered. The rest is unchanged: the receive side adds the rule
when the PPE reports the flow, and the ACKs refresh the session
through the ip_output probe.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/arht_kprobe.c |   14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/arht_kprobe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/arht_kprobe.c
@@ -65,6 +65,11 @@ static struct kprobe kp_ip6_local_out;
 static atomic_t skip_copy_kprobe_refcnt = ATOMIC_INIT(0);
 static DEFINE_MUTEX(skip_copy_kprobe_mutex);
 
+/* The tcp_recvmsg probe is shared with the wifi local-in code, so it
+ * needs to know when the dynamic IFC probes are registered.
+ */
+static bool difc_kprobes_active;
+
 
 /************************************************************************************************
 *
@@ -154,6 +159,13 @@ static int kp_tcp_recvmsg_pre(struct kpr
 		return 0;
 	}
 
+	/* A server socket of a listed application only receives, so the
+	 * tcp_sendmsg probe never sees it.
+	 */
+	if (READ_ONCE(difc_kprobes_active) && sk->sk_state == TCP_ESTABLISHED &&
+	    difc_is_current_app())
+		difc_add_entry_from_sock(sk);
+
 	if (READ_ONCE(sk->sk_mark) != SK_MARK_LOCAL_OFFLOAD){
 		return 0;
 	}
@@ -455,6 +467,7 @@ int arht_kprobe_difc_init(void)
 		goto err_unreg_v4_rcv;
 	}
 
+	WRITE_ONCE(difc_kprobes_active, true);
 	pr_info("arht_kprobe: all kprobes registered successfully!\n");
 	return 0;
 
@@ -486,6 +499,7 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL(arht_kprobe_difc_init);
 
 void arht_kprobe_difc_exit(void)
 {
+	WRITE_ONCE(difc_kprobes_active, false);
 	unregister_kprobe(&kp_tcp_v6_do_rcv);
 	unregister_kprobe(&kp_tcp_v4_do_rcv);
 	unregister_kprobe(&kp_ip6_local_out);
